    "text": "I did not submit a candidate. The file's change is real, but the profile doesn't show the new value, so I can't tell whether it's a deliberate new plan or junk.\n\n- **What changed:** Nothing structural. Same columns, same order, no missing or extra columns, and every other rule passes. The only failure is `plan_code`: 6 of 24 rows hold a value outside `[HMO, PPO, EPO, HDHP]`. The codes counts add to 18, which accounts for the 4 known codes. The other 6 rows carry a fifth value, and neither the profile nor the dry run shows what it is.\n- **Why I stopped:** Adding a code to `allowed` means naming it, and I can't see it. Guessing a value for a restricted healthcare feed would loosen the contract on evidence I don't have. Rejecting the file is the safe default meanwhile.\n- **Dry run on the unchanged contract:** accepted 0, rejected 6 (`VALUE.NOT_ALLOWED:plan_code` \u00d76), and the file is rejected as a whole (`FILE.BAD_ROW_RATIO`, 25% against a 5% limit). Validation passes with no loosening.\n- **Next step:** Ask the vendor (or whoever has the raw file) what the new `plan_code` value is and whether it's an intended plan type. If it is, I can add that value to `allowed` in a new version (version 2) and resubmit. If it's junk, the file should get a resend request instead.",
